cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RecoverBench, please cite the paper below. Please also credit MimicGen (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)."
title: "RecoverBench: A Systematic Benchmark for Error Recovery in Robotic Manipulation"
abstract: "RecoverBench evaluates how manipulation policies recover from standardized, reproducible post-error simulator states. It provides a taxonomy of 12 Error Skills (24 subtypes at two degrees, grouped into 5 Recovery Behavior Groups), 1,360 evaluation error scenes over six robosuite/MuJoCo tasks, a separate training scene pool, and a corpus of 10,598 recovery trajectories."
version: 1.1.0
